   "claim": "The W2-004 decision does not settle the 'raw' read named in D-086. Round 1 W2-004 asked for 'raw' to be dropped or recorded as (미확정)/post-v1, because docs/api/request.md has no raw body accessor. The decision only says wave 3 exposes no public body-reading method, so it is still open which accessor 'raw' means.",
   "evidence": "docs/research/naruserve-v1/waves/wave-3/design.md:53,114; docs/research/naruserve-v1/waves/wave-3/rounds/r1-merged.json (W2-004 suggested_fix)",
   "suggested_fix": "Add one clause to the body-ownership decision: v1 has no public raw body accessor, so 'raw' in D-086 refers only to internal reads of the body stream. BodyState enforces it for the readers that waves 5 and 6 add."
